  "notes": "Modified cash basis audit. Governmental receipts/disbursements from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances Total column (pp8-11; Total column on p9 and p11); the statement rolls forward fund balance (335,236 -> 385,377), which includes Due from Proprietary Funds 25,733, so fund balance is filled and beginning/ending cash left null as in FY2023 (governmental cash 353,128 + Cash at County Treasurer 6,516 at year end, p1/p7; no beginning cash printed). Transfers in/out from the Total column after the Adjustments column eliminations (p11). Statement 'Grants' 54,110 = General Fund 37,610 (printed as Federal Receipts on the budget schedule p20) + Park Fund 16,500 (grantor not printed); kept as one line. Business-type from the proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Fund Net Position Totals column (pp16-17), measure net position; no single total revenue line is printed, so business receipts total = operating + nonoperating revenues; disbursements total 1,003,344 printed on the Statement of Activities (p3) = operating 981,428 + interest 21,916. Proprietary cash flow statement (pp18-19) printed; proprietary left null as in the later years. Loan proceeds 116,007 (Trash Fund) appear only in the cash flow statement (p18). Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position (pp1-2) since it includes capital assets and debt; the Adjustments column is tagged fund_type eliminations. Government-wide restricted for grant expenditures 60,741 vs governmental funds balance sheet 60,471 (p7); the difference 270 is offset in Unrestricted (237,914 vs assigned 113,608 + unassigned 124,576); recorded as printed. Detail: budget comparison schedule (total primary government, pp20-21) revenue lines and business-type disbursement lines (Electric, Trash, Sewer, Water; no disbursement detail total since the governmental lines are left out); governmental disbursement detail from the more detailed Schedule of Expenditures by fund and object (p22; Grants Fund all zero) instead of the budget schedule's governmental function lines (General Government 208,526, Public Works 202,344, Culture and Recreation 109,280, which include transfers). Budget revenue 'Local Receipts: Other' 1,327,744 is mixed governmental and business-type. Electrical statistical data (p23) is not a money schedule. Read pages 1-23 of 23"
}
